// Name :
"P1981005982" "Basic Mission Goals"

// ToolTip :
"P2238007597" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Basic Mission Goals</color><br>Below is a list of possible goals. Select one of these goals to start adding different objectives to your mission. You can add more later on if you choose."





// Name :
"P30671714" "Fight a Boss"

// ToolTip :
"P2877024930" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Fight a Boss</color><br>This lets you place a Boss in the mission. The Boss can be as important or simple as you like. He can be the final fight at the end of the mission or just something cool to fight along the way.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br>The Boss, Frostfire, must be defeated in order for the player to successfully complete his mission.</color>"






// Name :
"P3284808684" "Collect an Object"

// ToolTip :
"P2775808545" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Collect an Object</color><br>This lets you place Objects on the mission map that players interact with (click). Objects have many potential uses such as clues for investigation, planted false evidence, or even prized items to be stolen or retrieved.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br>Break into that office and steal the credit card data off of their computers.</color>"







// Name :
"P2354967036" "Defeat All Enemies"

// ToolTip :
"P4107028897" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Defeat All Enemies</color><br>This lets you flag the mission as 'defeat all'. The player must sweep the entire mission map and defeat every last enemy in order to successfully complete his mission.<br><br>Defeat All Enemies ensures that the player stays in your map. Keep in mind, however, that forcing him to run around while he tracks down that final (and elusive) enemy can be a potentially frustrating experience."







// Name :
"P1985349211" "Free a Captive"

// ToolTip :
"P1950499102" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Free a Captive</color><br>This lets you flag the mission with a rescue opportunity. The Captive is a person that the player locates and frees. Once freed, the Captive immediately flees to the nearest door for safety.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown> Enter the abandoned warehouse and rescue Jane Marie.</color>"









// Name :
"P3149546515" "Advanced Mission Goals"

// ToolTip :
"P1565357126" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Advanced Mission Goals</color><br>Below is a more advanced list of goals. Select one of these goals to start adding different objectives to your mission. You can add more goals later if you like."





// Name :
"P12486503" "Add an Ally"

// ToolTip :
"P1584406892" "<color DeepSkyBlue>An Ally</color><br>This lets you add a 'friendly critter' to the mission who will follow the player around and help him fight.<br></color></color>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>Positron is surrounded by Malta. Once they're defeated, Positron stands up and says, 'Thanks, now let's shut this place down.' The player can then go through the rest of the mission with Positron by his side.</color>"








// Name :
"P2338823450" "Add an Ambush"

// ToolTip :
"P2453940541" "<color DeepSkyBlue>An Ambush</color><br>This lets you add an ambush to your mission. An ambush is a wave of critters who will chase after the player once an objective has been completed. Ambushes don't just happen. They need to be triggered, either by the player killing a Boss, clicking an Objective, or or some other goal flagged by you.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br>Once the final hostage has been rescued, a wave of Arachnos soldiers storm the mission map.</color>"








// Name :
"P1798429218" "Add an Escort"

// ToolTip :
"P852414379" "<color DeepSkyBlue>An Escort</color><br>This lets you add an NPC or 'friendly critter' to the mission who must be rescued and led to safety (exit). Escorts are dangerous because there's a chance that if a 'friendly critter' is used, it can be defeated and the player automatically fails the mission. However, Escort missions can also be set up as kidnappings, depending on the flavor text and animations you use.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown> Arachnos needs you to break into a tech lab and kidnap a Crey scientist.<br></color>"







// Name :
"P76210366" "Add a Patrol"

// ToolTip :
"P1348291679" "<color DeepSkyBlue>A Patrol</color><br>This lets you add a group of enemies flagged to wander an extended area of the mission map. These are good for making your map feel more alive as well as fleshing out the story of your mission.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br>As the player enters the map, he notices two guards walking around. One guard says, 'So, you think the boss is actually going through with it?' The other guard says, 'Between you and me, I hope not.'</color>"








// Name :
"P485020923" "Add a Battle"

// ToolTip :
"P3177962179" "<color DeepSkyBlue>A Battle</color><br>This lets you add two Enemy Groups to your mission to duke it out!<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown> Arachnos is invading a Longbow base and there are skirmishes between the two groups throughout the mission.<br></color>"








// Name :
"P3982757068" "Add a Destructible Object"

// ToolTip :
"P2155730869" "<color DeepSkyBlue>A Destructible Object</color><br>This lets you add a defeatable Object and its guards to your mission. You choose an Object, and the enemy guarding it, that the player will need to destroy.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br>Somewhere in this warehouse is a cursed relic that will doom the world if it's not destroyed.</color>"








// Name :
"P363527984" "Add a Defendable Object"

// ToolTip :
"P2792240289" "<color DeepSkyBlue>A Defendable Object</color><br>This lets you add an immobile Object to the mission that the player must to defend against a wave of attackers.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br>You need to protect the altar from the Circle of Thorns until the ritual is complete. If they destroy it, all the world is doomed!</color>"







// Name :
"P2218081262" "Add a Giant Monster"

// ToolTip :
"P1559586557" "<color DeepSkyBlue>A Giant Monster</color><br>RWAAARRR!!!!<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br>AHHHHHHH!</color>"













// DisplayName :
"P4255688915" "Story Settings"

// ToolTip :
"P3970747156" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Story Settings</color><br>The story settings are the overall settings for the story and all the missions contained in it."






