"P889412283" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Custom Character Group</color><br>The enemy group of which your custom-made character is a part."













// Name :
"P3357642543" "Contact Group"

// ToolTip :
"P1669198528" "<color DeepSkyBlue>About Contact</color><br>This is the group your contact will appear in if the player clicks to ask about this contact."








// Name :
"P851451980" "About Contact"

// ToolTip :
"P1434264975" "<color DeepSkyBlue>About Contact</color><br>This is the description of you contact that will appear if the player clicks to ask about this contact."










// Name :
"P349203958" "Story Parameters"

// ToolTip :
"P3535223800" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Story Parameters</color><br>This is where all of the optional aspects of the story are set.<br><br>Suggested Alignment:<color SandyBrown> The recommended alignment of the story. Note: this setting does not restrict players from doing this content. It only suggests a particular alignment to the player based off of your recommendation."





// Name :
"P1292801582" "Story Arc Status"

// ToolTip :
"P3732308473" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Story Arc Status</color><br>Declares the 'completion' state of a story. Other players will be able to see and search for these various states. Also, the status of Final is the only status eligible for a Dev Choice pick"








// Name :
"P1461992763" "Suggested Alignment"

// ToolTip :
"P2424255279" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Suggested Alignment</color><br>The recommended alignment of the story. Note: this setting does not restrict players from doing this content. It only suggests a particular alignment to the player based off of your recommendation.<br><br>Villianous:<color SandyBrown> Missions that have a villainous slant to them.</color><br>Heroic:<color SandyBrown> Missions that have a heroic slant to them.</color><br>Neutral: <color SandyBrown>Either a the mission has no particular alignment or the mission architect did not suggest one.</color>"









// Name :
"P2402446553" "Author Keyword Picks"

// ToolTip :
"P103944933" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Author Keyword Picks</color><br>As the author of the arc, you can pick the 3 best keywords you feel describe your arc."








// Name :
"P2025636931" "Souvenir Clue"

// ToolTip :
"P719666729" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Souvenir Clue</color><br>The clue given out at the end of the entire Story. You can find your Souvenir Clues by clicking the Clue button in the Navigation window and selecting the Architect Souvenirs tab.<br><br>A Souvenir Clue sums up the adventure and is meant as a reminder of the experience as a whole. Traditionally, Souvenir Clues are tied to a specific object that the player character collected during the course of the missions.<br><br>Shattered Glasses:<color SandyBrown> You look upon the broken pair of glasses and are reminded of the events you've come to know as <i>Time Enough at Last</i>. It all started when a simple bank teller went on break at work. He wanted to read and went into the vault for a little peace and quiet...<br></color>"





// Name :
"P1382292" "Souvenir Name"

// ToolTip :
"P747391188" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Souvenir Name</color><br>The name of the Souvenir Clue. Logically, this is the same as the name of the Story, but it doesn't have to be."






// Name :
"P1073433622" "Souvenir Description"

// ToolTip :
"P1097232882" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Souvenir Description</color><br>The actual Souvenir Clue text that will persist with the character forever (unless they choose to delete it)."













// DisplayName :
"P2967582626" "Choose Mission Settings"

// ToolTip :
"P2542853540" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Mission Settings</color><br><br>Enemy Group: <color SandyBrown>The enemies you want in your mission.<br></color>Map: <color SandyBrown>The map you want for your mission.</color><br>Optional Settings: <color SandyBrown>Not required for mission to be playable.</color><br><br><color red>Sections in <b>red</b> are required for the mission to be playable.</color>"






// ToolTip :
"P3707193155" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Enemy Group</color><br>There are two types of enemy groups, Standard and Custom.<br><br>Standard: These are enemies that are already existing in the game, created by the developers.<br><br>Custom: These are enemy groups that you, the architect, have created."



// ReplaceNoneWith :
"P2713311984" "None Selected"




// DisplayName :
"P3917592017" "Standard"






// ToolTip :
"P2769387642" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Enemy Group</color><br>Select the enemy group for your mission. These enemies will automatically be placed throughout your map.<br><br>The two numbers in parenthesis (#-#) are the level ranges of the enemy group. You will have to keep all enemies, allies and bosses within the same level range in order for the mission to be playable.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br>Selecting '5th Column' will make all the default enemies on the map 5th Column units. Because their level range is from 1 - 54 there are no restrictions on the rest of the mission.</color>"







// DisplayName :
"P4062712749" "Custom"





// Name :
"P2370434884" "Custom Group"

// ToolTip :
"P3518430535" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Custom Groups</color><br>Select the custom group for your mission. These enemies will automatically be placed throughout your map.<br><br>The two numbers in parenthesis (#-#) are the level range of the enemy group. You will have to keep all enemies, allies and bosses within the same level range in order for the mission to be playable.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br>Selecting '5th Column' will make all the default enemies on the map 5th Column units. Because their level range is from 1 - 54 there are no restrictions on the rest of the mission.</color>"













// Name :
"P1026575050" "Map Type"

// ToolTip :
"P111453729" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Map Type</color><br>Select the map for your mission."









// Name :
"P995260592" "Mission Parameters"

// ToolTip :
"P1801577270" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Mission Settings</color><br>These settings are not required for the mission to be playable.<br><br>Mission Pacing:<color SandyBrown> Pacing controls the level range progression of enemies on a map.</color><br>Time to Complete:<color SandyBrown> Adds a time limit to the mission.</color>"





// Name :
"P1445377620" "Minimum Level"

// ToolTip :
"P113274839" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Minimum Level</color><br>This is the minimum level your mission will be playable at.  Players lower than this level will be auto-sidekicked to this level, but critters lower than this level will not be brought up.  It may mean grey conning enemies will appear in your mission."







// Name :
"P376032802" "Maximum Level"

// ToolTip :
"P489206411" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Maximum Level</color><br>This is the max level you mission will be playable at.  Players higher than this level will be auto-exemplared to this level.  <color ArchitectError>Warning, critters that usually spawn at higher levels will be brought down as well.  They may be much too powerful for a low level character!"








// Name :
"P3500142445" "Mission Pacing"

// ToolTip :
"P789025352" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Mission Pacing</color><br>Mission Pacing controls the level range progression of enemies on a map.<br><br>Back Loaded:<color SandyBrown> Lower level enemies are in the front of the mission and higher level enemies are in the back.</color><br>Flat: <color SandyBrown>Enemies level ranges are evenly spread throughout a mission map (default).<br></color>Ramp Up:<color SandyBrown> The mission map slowly goes up in levels as players go further into the mission.<br></color>Staggered: The level range of the enemies goes up and down throughout the map.</color>"







// Name :
"P3330294222" "Time to Complete"

// ToolTip :
"P3392262036" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Time to Complete</color><br>This sets the amount of time the player has to complete this mission in minutes. The default is turned off.<br><br>Setting a timer creates potential for the player to fail the mission. Failing the mission still progresses the player to the next mission, but he doesn't receive as many rewards. <br><br>Also, make sure to add <i>Mission Failure Text</i> and dialog into the mission."




// DisplayName :
"P3050699932" "There is no time limit on this mission."





