// Name :
"P2372826327" "Mission Begin Clue"


// ToolTip :
"P1906708643" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Mission Begin Clue</color><br>This is a clue that is given at the start of the mission. A clue is usually text that reveals some deeper aspect of the story to the player."



// Name :
"P2125455069" "Clue Name"

// ToolTip :
"P3738419953" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Clue Name</color><br>The name of the clue given when the player starts this mission."






// Name :
"P152630490" "Clue Description"

// ToolTip :
"P478452396" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Clue Description</color><br>The text of the clue given when the player starts this mission."








// Name :
"P3336338855" "Mission Complete Clue"


// ToolTip :
"P2391605295" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Mission Complete Clue</color><br>This is a clue that is given at the end of the mission. A clue is usually text that reveals some deeper aspect of the story to the player."




// ToolTip :
"P3115039932" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Clue Name</color><br>The name of the clue given when the player has completed this mission."







// ToolTip :
"P1292077831" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Clue Description</color><br>The text of the clue given when the player has completed this mission."













// DisplayName :
"P2458990516" "Write Text"

// ToolTip :
"P3814113753" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Write Text</color><br>This is where you'll write most of the text and dialog for your mission.<br><br><color red>Sections in <b>red</b> are required for the mission to be playable.</color>"





// Name :
"P4254605386" "Mission Introduction Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P1073732984" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Mission Introduction Dialog</color><br>The first dialog the player reads regarding the mission. It's spoken by the Contact to the player.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>I really need your help with something. There's this guy... and, uh, he's doing something really bad. Can you help me?</color>"








// Name :
"P381861420" "Mission Send Off Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P724572821" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Mission Send Off Dialog</color><br>The dialog the player reads after they accept the mission from the contact. It's spoken by the contact to the player.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>Thank you so much for helping me. This guy hangs out in this old office building. His name's Frostfire; he's a member of the Outcasts.</color>"








// Name :
"P1399135934" "Compass Active Task Text"

// ToolTip :
"P5613982" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Compass Active Task Text</color><br>This is a short description displayed in the navigation bar while the player is on the mission. This dialog should be short and to the point.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>Defeat Frostfire</color>"

// Default :
"P0" ""








// Name :
"P502170569" "Still Busy Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P324938060" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Still Busy Dialog</color><br>The dialog given by the Contact if the player returns to them but has yet to complete the mission. This is the 'you still need to take care of that thing I asked you to do' dialog.<br><br>Sometimes a player returns to the Contact before completing the mission because they're lost or confused. Use this dialog block to help refocus them.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>Oh, hi. How is it going with Frostfire? I've heard that he is still in that abandoned office building with all the rest of the Outcasts. I hope you're still up for going after him. I'd hate to think of all the trouble he'd cause if he was allowed to roam free.</color>"








// Name :
"P154629560" "Return Success Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P2962217292" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Return Success Dialog</color><br>The dialog given by the contact when the player returns to them after successfully completing the mission. Generally, this is the 'Well done' or 'That's an interesting piece of information you gathered' dialog.<br><br>If there are missions after this one, consider using the Return Success Dialog as a bridge to the Mission Introduction Dialog for the next mission.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>You took out Frostfire? Wow, that's amazing. Did he happen to say anything about my sister? That's the real reason I asked you to go in there... she's missing.</color>"








// Name :
"P1181403063" "Additional Text"

// ToolTip :
"P365531013" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Additional Text</color><br>This section has other text options you can add to your mission, but are not needed for it to be playable."





// Name :
"P862715059" "Mission Title"

// ToolTip :
"P740850530" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Mission Title</color><br>Title of the individual mission displayed in the dialog window.<br><br>Example: <color SandyBrown>Extinguish Frostfire</color>"







// Name :
"P2552922919" "Mission Subtitle"

// ToolTip :
"P3462353641" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Mission Title</color><br>Subtitle, displayed directly beneath the Title in the dialog window.<br><br>Example: <color SandyBrown>Part One.</color>"







// Name :
"P2874580579" "Mission Accept Text"

// ToolTip :
"P310871727" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Mission Title</color><br>The short line the player clicks to accept the mission. Generally, this is simply Accept, but it can be anything.<br><br>Example: <color SandyBrown>I agree to help you take out Frostfire.</color>"


// Default :
"P3029133314" "Accept"






// Name :
"P620706377" "Mission Entry Popup"

// ToolTip :
"P3468343518" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Mission Entry Popup</color><br>The popup window that appears when the player enters the mission map.<br><br>Example: <color SandyBrown>You can tell by the faint smell of death that creeps into your nostrils, that this is going to get messy.</color>"








// Name :
"P3985222173" "Mission Success Popup"

// ToolTip :
"P1068860783" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Mission Success Popup</color><br>The popup window that appears when the player exits a mission that they've successfully completed.<br><br>Example: <color SandyBrown>Now that Frostfire is defeated, the sun seems to shine a little brighter as you step back onto the city streets.</color>"








// Name :
"P3227426206" "Mission Fail Popup"

// ToolTip :
"P1000004730" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Mission Fail Popup</color><br>The popup window that appears when the player exits a mission they've failed to complete.<br><br>Example: <color SandyBrown>Frostfire got away and now you must return to Mary Contrary (Contact) with your head hung low.</color>"








// Name :
"P3824003569" "Return Fail Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P3449159315" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Return Fail Dialog</color><br>Dialog spoken by the contact when the player returns having failed the mission. If there is a mission after this, the StoryArc will still progress.<br><br>Example: <color SandyBrown>Frostfire got away... no. It can't be. You were supposed to-- I'm sorry, I'm just really worried. You see, he kidnapped my sister and I was hoping that you'd be able to help me."














// DisplayName :
"P2416614906" "Ambush"

// ToolTip :
"P2793249375" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Ambush</color><br>Ambushes are triggered off of other goals. Once triggered, an ambush will chase players throughout the map."








