// Name :
"P473154195" "Settings"

// ToolTip :
"P1230210459" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Ambush Settings</color><br>These settings are not required for the mission to be playable."






// ToolTip :
"P939426191" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Enemy Group</color><br>There are two types of enemies you can select from.<br><br>Standard: <color SandyBrown>Enemies that already exist in the game.</color><br><br>.Custom: <color SandyBrown>Enemies that you create using the custom enemy creator.</color>"











// Name :
"P591301051" "Ambush Enemy Group"

// ToolTip :
"P939442325" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Ambush Enemy Group</color><br>The enemy group you want for the ambush."


// ReplaceNoneWith :
"P2780899354" "Same As Mission"













// ToolTip :
"P2850423075" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Custom Group</color><br>Custom Groups are groups of enemies, allies or civilians that you've created for Mission Architect."













// Name :
"P2791125050" "Ambush Alignment"

// ToolTip :
"P1870564715" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Ambush Alignment</color><br>Sets the alignment of the enemy group ambushing the player. Alignment determines what 'team' the enemy group is on during the mission.<br><br>Ally: <color SandyBrown>The ambush will actually be your friend and the the enemy of all other spawns on the map.</color><br>Enemy: <color SandyBrown>The ambush is the enemy of the player, but not the of the rest of the spawns on the map. Default.</color><br>Rogue: <color SandyBrown>The ambush is no one's friend. Not yours or the other enemies on the map. They'll fight everything they come across. "








// Name :
"P523253932" "Ambush Difficulty"

// ToolTip :
"P1240756332" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Ambush Difficulty</color><br>The difficulty of the enemies in the ambush. Increasing the difficulty adds enemies of higher ranks into the ambush, more lieutenants as opposed to minions or more bosses as opposed to lieutenants, etc."









// Name :
"P1120787796" "Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P3173638902" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Dialog</color><br>Text and dialog that you can add to an ambush, but are not required for the ambush to be playable."





// Name :
"P3585149149" "Ambush Creation Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P3548877372" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Ambush Creation Dialog</color><br>The dialog spoken by the ambush as soon as the appear on the map.<br><br>Example: <color SandyBrown>Attack!</color>"













// DisplayName :
"P2664220932" "Boss"

// ToolTip :
"P2704942724" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss</color><br>A boss is a significant enemy you want the players to face. He could be placed at the end of the map and defeating him completes the mission or she could be placed somewhere else in the map to add to the story or difficulty and not be required for mission complete."








// Name :
"P1359223233" "Boss Name"

// ToolTip :
"P1649216245" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss Name</color><br>This is where you put the name of your boss.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br><i>The Big Bad.<br>Mr. Goody Two Shoes</i></color>"








// Name :
"P2214146286" "Boss Type"

// ToolTip :
"P3999123565" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss Type</color><br>The type of boss you want the player to have. You have two options here.<br><br>Standard: <color SandyBrown>All the bosses that are currently being used in the game.</color><br>Custom Boss: <color SandyBrown>A custom boss made by you."











// Name :
"P4219912035" "Boss Enemy Group"

// ToolTip :
"P1029455087" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss Enemy Group</color><br>The enemy group of which your boss is a part. Selecting an enemy group allows you to choose the specific boss you want for this goal. <br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br><i>Selecting 5th Column allows you to then choose Requiem as a specific enemy.</i></color>"






























// Name :
"P154993707" "Boss Settings"

// ToolTip :
"P295343735" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss Settings</color><br>These settings aren't required for your boss to playable."





// Name :
"P2363474820" "Required for Mission Complete"

// ToolTip :
"P1470978865" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Required for Mission Complete</color><br>If this option is turned on, the mission goal must be completed for the mission to complete. If it's turned off, the player does not need to defeat the boss in order for the mission to complete."






// DisplayName :
"P1563333174" "Required for Mission Completion"







// Name :
"P2921299587" "This Mission Goal is created when..."

// ToolTip :
"P1894335046" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Chain Mission Goals</color><br>You can link different mission goals together, creating a chain of events that occur one after the next. Setting this option makes it so this mission goal won't appear until the previous goal is completed. This allows for you to cascade objectives in a mission.<br><br><color SandyBrown>Example: A player completes a collection objective by finding the final chest, just then the Boss spawns ranting about his alarm system always going off.</color>"




// // :
"P4273580311" "Mission Begins"





// Name :
"P1720022112" "Quantity"

// ToolTip :
"P4111004844" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Quantity</color><br>The number of this type of boss you want to have in your mission. This will make multiple copies of this boss in the mission.<br><br>Note that if you use this option, the costume, dialog, alignment, placement, starting animation, all of it will be exactly the same. Traditionally, this is only useful for the more generic bosses you want to have in a map to fill out the space."







// Name :
"P2923404543" "Alignment"

// ToolTip :
"P2740431591" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Alignment</color><br>Sets the alignment of your boss. Alignment determines what 'team' the boss is going to be on during the mission.<br><br>Ally: <color SandyBrown>The boss will actually be your friend and the the enemy of all other spawns on the map.</color><br>Enemy: <color SandyBrown>The boss is the enemy of the player, but not the of the rest of the spawns on the map. Default.</color><br>Rogue: <color SandyBrown>The boss is no one's friend. Not yours or the other enemies on the map. They'll fight everything they come across."








// Name :
"P260424405" "Boss Placement"

// ToolTip :
"P3369181906" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss Placement</color><br>The location on the map that the boss will spawn.<br><br>Any: <color SandyBrown>The game will pick a random location from Front, Middle or Back to appear.</color><br>Back: <color SandyBrown>The boss will spawn in the back of the mission map.</color><br>Front: <color SandyBrown>The boss will spawn in the front of the map.</color><br>Middle: <color SandyBrown>The boss will spawn in the middle of the map.</color>"








// Name :
"P1800146608" "Enemy Group Difficulty"

// ToolTip :
"P1100159560" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Difficulty</color><br>The level of difficulty of the enemies with the boss, not the difficulty of the boss itself. Increasing the difficulty adds enemies of higher ranks into the boss spawn, more lieutenants as opposed to minions or more bosses as opposed to lieutenants, etc."





















// Name :
"P2324184175" "Surrounding Enemy Group"

// ToolTip :
"P2331116237" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Surrounding Enemy Group</color><br>The enemy group of which your boss is a part. Selecting an enemy group allows you to choose the specific boss you want for this mission goal. <br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br><i>Selecting 5th Column allows you to then choose Requiem as a specific enemy.</i></color>"





// ReplaceNoneWith :
"P2071074472" "Same As Boss"
























// Name :
"P632451536" "Boss Starting Animation"

// ToolTip :
"P387653794" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Starting Animation</color><br>The animation of the boss when first encountered.<br><br>Note: Regretfully, not all animations work for all entities."








// Name :
"P1023358296" "Enemy Group Starting Animation"

// ToolTip :
"P2824955898" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Enemy Group Starting Animation</color><br>The animation the rest of the group attached to the boss is doing. All enemies in this groups will be doing this animation when a player approaches them.<br><br>Note: Regretfully, not all animations work for all entities."









// Name :
"P808855328" "Boss Flees on Damage"

// ToolTip :
"P682673272" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss Flees on Damage</color><br>The boss will attempt to flee the mission when their hit points drop to this percentage. The player will have to chase them down before they reach the exit. If the boss reaches the exit, the player will fail the mission. This means you'll have to fill out the Return Fail Dialog for this mission.<br><br>Note, there are certain bosses who will flee from the players regardless of this being set. In these cases the boss doesn't attempt to exit the mission, merely run away from the players.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>Setting this number to 50 means that when the boss has lost 50%% of their hit points he'll attempt to exit the mission.</color>"




// DisplayName :
"P3983355187" "Boss does not flee (for health reasons)."






// DisplayName :
"P3811360262" "Boss flees at full health."





// DisplayName :
"P2183407804" "Boss flees at 75%% health."





// DisplayName :
"P524819041" "Boss flees at 50%% health."





// DisplayName :
"P445079468" "Boss flees at 25%% health."





// DisplayName :
"P474882334" "Boss flees at 10%% health."





// DisplayName :
"P3019450110" "Boss flees at 5%% health."








// Name :
"P2366452416" "Boss Flees on Minion Defeats"

// ToolTip :
"P3450130285" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss Flees on Minon Defeats</color><br>The boss will attempt to flee the mission when the minions in their encounter group drop to this number. This means the mission can be failed and therefore, you'll have to write some Return Fail Dialog for your story contact.<br><br>In a single player mission, most bosses will only have two other spawns with them. In a mission with a party of 8 that count can go up to a dozen. For this to work correctly in a single player mission you'll have to keep the count at 1. If you raise it higher than that the boss will start in a flee state (which also might be your intended goal).<br><br>Note, there are certain bosses who will flee from the players regardless of this being set. In these cases the boss doesn't attempt to exit the mission, merely run away from the players.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>Setting this number to 1 means that when the boss has only one minion left in his group, he'll attempt to exit the mission.</color>"





// DisplayName :
"P1292896925" "Boss does not flee (for minion defeat reasons)."






// DisplayName :
"P3768066464" "Boss flees when only 1 minion remains."





// DisplayName :
"P1536388214" "Boss flees when only 2 minions remain."





// DisplayName :
"P3694503733" "Boss flees when only 3 minions remain."





// DisplayName :
"P1776567470" "Boss flees whenh only 4 minions remain."





// DisplayName :
"P2063667261" "Boss flees when only 5 minions remain."





// DisplayName :
"P681266105" "Boss flees when only 6 minions remain."






// DisplayName :
"P2940043514" "Boss flees when only 7 minions remain."





// DisplayName :
"P1774170927" "Boss flees when only 8 minions remain."





// DisplayName :
"P3994646636" "Boss flees when only 9 minions remain."





// DisplayName :
"P3836729683" "Boss flees when only 10 minions remain."





// DisplayName :
"P1661538832" "Boss flees when only 11 minions remain."





// DisplayName :
"P814958996" "Boss flees when only 12 minions remain."








// Name :
"P3088998689" "Boss Run Away Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P964804664" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss Run Away Dialog</color><br>The dialog spoken by the boss when they decide to run away.<br><br>Example:<br><i><color SandyBrown>I'm outta here!</i></color>"







// Name :
"P1811004186" "Defeat Condition"

// ToolTip :
"P1739037982" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Defeat Condition</color><br>This states what the player needs to do in order for the boss to be considered defeated. There are currently two options.<br><br>Only Boss: <color SandyBrown>The player only needs to defeat the boss, not the rest of the enemies with the encounter.</color><br>Entire Encounter: <color SandyBrown>The player has to defeat the boss and the rest of the enemies with the encounter in order for the boss to be considered defeated.</color>"




// DisplayName :
"P280145310" "Only Boss needed to complete"





// DisplayName :
"P3463840094" "Entire Encounter needed to complete"











// Name :
"P883736576" "Boss Text"

// ToolTip :
"P413081859" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss Text</color><br>Text associated with the boss that's not required for the mission to be playable."





// Name :
"P1758409905" "Boss Group"

// ToolTip :
"P1233900738" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss group</color><br>This is where you put the group of your boss.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br><i>The Big Bad.<br>Mr. Goody Two Shoes</i></color>"








// Name :
"P1512914307" "Boss Description"

// ToolTip :
"P2772807531" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss Description</color><br>The description or bio of your boss. The description is given when a player right-clicks on the boss and selects info.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br><i>Frostfire was once a hero, but has taken a dark path and found himself leader of a gang called the Outcasts.</i></color>"








// Name :
"P1215555202" "Navigation Text (Plural)"

// ToolTip :
"P4031626825" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Navigation Text (Plural)</color><br>The short description displayed in the navigation bar that pertains specifically to this boss. This is the 'plural' description, meaning it's only used if you have more than one of this boss in the mission (if you set your quantity to something greater than 1). A number is automatically placed in front of this description, so format your text appropriately.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>3 Outcast Bosses to Defeat<br>6 of Frostfire's Bosses Remain<br>2 Bosses to question</color>"







// Name :
"P4076396695" "Navigation Text (Singular)"

// ToolTip :
"P2222240383" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Navigation Text (Singular)</color><br>The short description displayed in the navigation bar that pertains specially to this boss. This is the 'singular' description, meaning it's used only if you have <b>one</b> boss of this type (if you kept the quantity of this boss set at one or if there is only one left in the mission).<br><br>Unlike the plural version of this description, the singular does not place a number in front of the text. So, you'll have to add it in if that's what you want.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>1 Outcast Boss Remains<br>Defeat Last Boss<br>Only 1 more left...</color>"







// Name :
"P1366413467" "Boss Defeated Text"

// ToolTip :
"P3166652708" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss Defeated Text</color><br>This text displays in the chat window when the boss is defeated.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>You have defeated Frostfire. Return to your contact for further instruction.</color>"






// Name :
"P3437205676" "Boss Unaware Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P4014914919" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss Unaware Dialog</color><br>The dialog spoken by the boss when they are unaware of the player character. This fires off as the players approach the boss.<br><br>Example:<br><i><color SandyBrown>It's about time the Outcasts took what was rightfully theirs.</i></color>"







// Name :
"P2728036334" "Boss Attack Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P2283128240" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss Attack Dialog</color><br>The dialog spoken by the boss when they are aware of the player character.<br><br>Example:<br><i><color SandyBrown>Ah, I figured some hero or another would try and stop us. Impossible!</i></color>"







// Name :
"P2485820726" "Player Deals Damage to Boss Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P4011498691" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Player Deals Damage to Boss Dialog</color><br>The dialog spoken by the boss the first time the player deals damage to boss.<br><br>Example:<br><i><color SandyBrown>You hit like a girl... a really strong girl.</i></color>"







// Name :
"P3892811061" "Boss At 3/4 Health"

// ToolTip :
"P1556566811" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss At 3/4 Health</color><br>The dialog spoken when the boss is at 3/4 health.<br><br>Example:<br><i><color SandyBrown>Is that the best you can do?</i></color>"







// Name :
"P386494499" "Boss 1/2 Health"

// ToolTip :
"P2432473008" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss 1/2 Health</color><br>The dialog spoken when the boss is at 1/2 health.<br><br>Example:<br><i><color SandyBrown>Maybe I under estimated you.</i></color>"







// Name :
"P3513153956" "Boss 1/4 Health"

// ToolTip :
"P1571243054" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss 1/4 Health</color><br>The dialog spoken when the boss is at 1/4 health.<br><br>Example:<br><i><color SandyBrown>I'm not feeling so well...</i></color>"







// Name :
"P890632964" "Boss Is Defeated Dialog"



// ToolTip :
"P125594859" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss Is Defeated</color><br>The dialog spoken when the boss is defeated.<br><br>Example:<br><i><color SandyBrown>So cold... it burns...</i></color>"






// Name :
"P2625603592" "Boss Defeated Player Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P4269853282" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss Defeated Player</color><br>The dialog spoken when the boss defeats the player character.<br><br>Example:<br><i><color SandyBrown>How you like them apples?</i></color>"








// Name :
"P1282464397" "Boss Defeated Clue"


// ToolTip :
"P2507507985" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss Defeated Clue</color><br>The clue granted on defeat of the boss. Clues are helpful to progress the story, giving more information directly related to the Boss."




// ToolTip :
"P2565205188" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Clue Name</color><br>The name of the clue that appears in the clue window for the player. <br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>Frostfire Talks<br>Questioning Frostfire<br>The plot thickens</color>"







// ToolTip :
"P3779880706" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Clue Description</color><br>The actual text of the clue. The player will get this description from their clue window.<br><br>Example: <color SandyBrown>Upon defeating Frostfire he told you, '<i>I don't know anything about this missing kid. I don't know what your contact told you, but it wasn't the Outcasts who kidnapped her.</i>'</color>"













// DisplayName :
"P112405066" "Giant Monster"

// ToolTip :
"P3005327099" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Boss</color><br>A giant monster is a significant enemy you want the players to face. He could be placed at the end of the map and defeating him completes the mission or she could be placed somewhere else in the map to add to the story or difficulty and not be required for mission complete."








// Name :
"P2486713920" "Giant Monster Name"

// ToolTip :
"P4183731325" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Giant Monster Name</color><br>This is where you put the name of your Giant Monster.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br><i>The Big Bad.<br>Mr. Goody Two Shoes</i></color>"









