// ToolTip :
"P173518173" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Chain Mission Goals</color><br>You can link different mission goals together, creating a chain of events that occur one after the next. Setting this option makes it so this mission goal won't appear until the previous goal is completed. This allows for you to cascade objectives in a mission.<br><br><color SandyBrown>Example: A player completes a collection objective by finding the final chest, just then the Giant Monster spawns ranting about his alarm system always going off.</color>"










// ToolTip :
"P2183908627" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Quantity</color><br>The number of this type of Giant Monster you want to have in your mission. This will make multiple copies of this Giant Monster in the mission.<br><br>Note that if you use this option, the costume, dialog, alignment, starting animation, all of it will be exactly the same. Traditionally, this is only useful for the more generic Giant Monster you want to have in a map to fill out the space."








// ToolTip :
"P2094623680" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Alignment</color><br>Sets the alignment of your Giant Monster. Alignment determines what 'team' the Giant Monster is going to be on during the mission.<br><br>Ally: <color SandyBrown>The boss will actually be your friend and the the enemy of all other spawns on the map.</color><br>Enemy: <color SandyBrown>The boss is the enemy of the player, but not the of the rest of the spawns on the map. Default.</color><br>Rogue: <color SandyBrown>The Giant Monster is no one's friend. Not yours or the other enemies on the map. They'll fight everything they come across."









