// DisplayName :
"P3004196578" "Collection"

// ToolTip :
"P1400483791" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Collection</color><br>This lets you place objects on the map players get to interact with (click). These are good for investigation missions as well as planting false evidence or theft missions.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br>Break into that office and steal the credit card data off of their computers.</color>"








// Name :
"P1193391190" "Collection Name"

// ToolTip :
"P2336735964" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Collection Name</color><br>The name of the object the player will interact with. When a player clicks on the object, this is the name that will appear above the object in the game.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>Computer Desk<br>Display Case<br>Body Bag</color>"








// Name :
"P2514263417" "Collection Type"

// ToolTip :
"P4033064648" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Collection Type</color><br>Collection objects are broken down into two types.<br><br>Floor: <color SandyBrown>Objects that can be placed on the floor.</color><br>Wall: <color SandyBrown>Objects that must be placed against a wall.</color><br><br>Once you've selected the type of object you can then choose the actual Collection Object for you mission."










// ToolTip :
"P1584309611" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Settings</color><br>These settings are not required for the mission."





// ToolTip :
"P2988075979" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Required for Mission Complete</color><br>If this option is turned on, the mission goal must be completed for the mission to complete. If it's turned off, the player does not need to interact with this object in order for the mission to complete."















// ToolTip :
"P657518306" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Quantity</color><br>The number of this specific object you want in your mission. This will make multiple copies of the same object.<br><br>Note that if you use this option, the object, description, placement, all of it will be exactly the same. Traditionally, this is only useful for the more generic objects you want to have in a map to fill out the space."








// Name :
"P2582146370" "Object Placement"

// ToolTip :
"P805625716" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Object Placement</color><br>The location on the map that the object will appear.<br><br>Any: <color SandyBrown>The game will pick a random location from Front, Middle or Back to appear.</color><br>Back: <color SandyBrown>The object will appear in the back of the mission map.</color><br>Front: <color SandyBrown>The object will appear in the front of the map.</color><br>Middle: <color SandyBrown>The object will appear in the middle of the map.</color>"







// Name :
"P1256200488" "Interact Time"

// ToolTip :
"P3196449168" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Interact Time</color><br>The time in seconds the player has to wait after clicking on the object before it is considered complete."








// Name :
"P3251828722" "Remove Object on Complete"

// ToolTip :
"P4257529027" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Remove Object on Complete</color><br>Selecting Remove on Complete will cause the object to disappear once the player has interacted with it."





// DisplayName :
"P2550859399" "Remove On Complete"






// DisplayName :
"P3873336300" "Do Not Remove On Complete"







// Name :
"P3430768944" "This Collection becomes active when..."

// ToolTip :
"P1349418659" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Chain Mission Goals</color><br>You can link different mission goals together, creating a chain of events that occur one after the next. Setting this option makes it so this mission goal won't activate until the previous goal is completed. This allows for you to cascade objectives in a mission.<br><br><color SandyBrown>Example: A player completes a collection objective by finding the final chest, just then the Boss spawns ranting about his chest alarm system always going off.</color>"








// Name :
"P3738814544" "Object Fades In"

// ToolTip :
"P3741838107" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Object Fades In</color><br>If Object Fades In is selected the object will appear translucent until the object is clicked.  This is commonly used to give the impression the player is placing an item that is not there rather than interacting with a pre-existing item."





// DisplayName :
"P3546647780" "Object Does Not Fade In"















// Name :
"P2612594937" "Text"


// ToolTip :
"P1587674339" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Collection Text</color><br>This text is not required for the mission."





// ToolTip :
"P1920235011" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Navigation Text (Plural)</color><br>The short description displayed in the navigation bar that pertains specifically to this object. This is the 'plural' description, meaning it's only used if you have more than one of this specific object in the mission (if you set your quantity to something greater than 1).<br><br>A number is automatically placed in front of this description, so format your text appropriately.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>3 Desks to Search<br>6 Files Remaining<br>2 Plans to Steal</color>"









// ToolTip :
"P3947660352" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Navigation Text (Singular)</color><br>The short description displayed in the navigation bar that pertains specially to this object. This is the 'singular' description, meaning it's used only if you have <b>one</b> object of this type (if you kept the quantity of this object set at one or if there is only one left in the mission).<br><br>Unlike the plural version of this description, the singular does not place a number in front of the text. So, you'll have to add it in if that's what you want.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>1 Computer Remains<br>Find Last Journal<br>Only 1 Safe Left...</color>"








// Name :
"P2156697384" "Begin Interaction Text"

// ToolTip :
"P2005770718" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Begin Interaction Text</color><br>This text displays in the chat window when the player begins interacting with a collection object.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>You begin searching for hidden computer files.</color>"







// Name :
"P928467803" "Interrupt Interaction Text"

// ToolTip :
"P1069930480" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Interrupt Interaction Text</color><br>This text displays in the chat window when the player is interrupted from interacting with a collection object.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>You've been interrupted.</color>"







// Name :
"P1315709471" "Complete Interaction Text"

// ToolTip :
"P1877548270" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Complete Interaction Text</color><br>This text displays in the chat window when the player has completed interacting with this single object.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>You found some hidden computer files.</color>"







// Name :
"P3457637641" "Interact Bar Text"



// ToolTip :
"P1528422866" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Interact Bar Text</color><br>This text displays over the top of the interact bar after the player clicks on the object. <br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>Searching for files...</color>"







// Name :
"P3173404979" "Collection Completed Clue"


// ToolTip :
"P864874674" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Collection Completed Clue</color><br>This clue is granted to the player once they've interacted with the object. Clues are helpful to progress the story, giving more information directly related to this object."




// ToolTip :
"P1875339353" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Clue Name</color><br>The name of the clue that appears in the clue window for the player. <br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>Hidden Files<br>Safe Combination<br>Forgotten Journal</color>"







// ToolTip :
"P1003526260" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Clue Description</color><br>The actual text of the clue. The player will get this description once they've interacted with this object.<br><br>Example: <color SandyBrown>These documents reveal a secret plan by a senior lieutenant of the Outcasts to kidnap a girl and sell her to the Circle of Thorns. It appears that Frostfire doesn't know anything about this rogue group within his gang.</color>"













// DisplayName :
"P1885571446" "A Defendable Object"

// Tooltip :
"P438374681" "<color DeepSkyBlue>A Defendable Object</color><br>An immobile object the players have to defend from a wave of attackers.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br>You need to protect the altar from the Circle of Thorns until the ritual is complete. If they destroy it, all the world is doomed.</color>"








// Name :
"P878141227" "Defend Object List"

// ToolTip :
"P3287912967" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Defend Object List</color><br>The list of possible objects that can be defended.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>Ancient Lockbox<br>Clockwork Parts<br>Ancient Tablet</color>"









// Name :
"P784128309" "Defend Object Name"

// ToolTip :
"P1390131514" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Defend Object Name</color><br>The name of the object. Players will see this name when they click on the object. It will also be the name you will use when sending the players into the mission to defend said object.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>Ancient Lockbox<br>Medical Equipment<br>All Your Worldly Possessions.</color>"










// ToolTip :
"P2606253359" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Settings</color><br>These settings are not required for this mission goal to be playable."





// ToolTip :
"P2082261569" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Required for Mission Complete</color><br>If this option is turned on, the mission goal must be completed for the mission to complete. If it's turned off, the player does not need to defend this object in order for the mission to complete."














// ToolTip :
"P3002937303" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Chain Mission Goals</color><br>You can link different mission goals together, creating a chain of events that occur one after the next. Setting this option makes it so this mission goal won't appear until the previous goal is completed. This allows for you to cascade objectives in a mission.<br><br><color SandyBrown>Example: A player completes a collection objective by finding the final chest, just then the Boss spawns ranting about his chest alarm system always going off.</color>"









// ToolTip :
"P2453335570" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Quantity</color><br>The number of this type of defendable objects you want to in your mission. This will make multiple copies of this object in the mission.<br><br>Note that if you use this option, the object, description, placement, all of it will be exactly the same. Traditionally, this is only useful for the more generic objects you want to have in a map to fill out the space."



















// Name :
"P1210429558" "Attacking Enemy Group"

// ToolTip :
"P2953127859" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Attacking Enemy Group</color><br>The enemy group attacking the object."



























// Name :
"P710122716" "Mission Goal Alignment"

// ToolTip :
"P1629170807" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Mission Goal Alignment</color><br>Sets the alignment of the entire Mission goal, including the object meant to be defended, the guards around the object and the attacking enemies. Alignment determines what 'team' the enemy group is on during the mission.<br><br>Ally: <color SandyBrown>The enemy group will actually be your friend and the the enemy of all other spawns on the map.</color><br>Enemy: <color SandyBrown>The enemy group is the enemy of the player, but not the of the rest of the spawns on the map. Default.</color><br>Rogue: <color SandyBrown>The enemy group is no one's friend. Not yours or the other enemies on the map. They'll fight everything they come across.<br><br>In both Enemy and Rogue alignment choices, the object can be destroyed and therefore this mission goal can be failed."
















// ToolTip :
"P3987612121" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Enemy Group Difficulty</color><br>The difficulty of the enemies attacking the object. Increasing the difficulty adds enemies of higher ranks into the group, more lieutenants as opposed to minions or more bosses as opposed to lieutenants, etc."









// ToolTip :
"P1514598260" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Enemy Group Starting Animation</color><br>The animation the enemy group is doing as the player approaches them. All enemies in this groups will be doing this animation.<br><br>Note: Regretfully, not all animations work for all entities."









// Name :
"P1286552112" "Text & Dialog"


// ToolTip :
"P2490491988" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Defend Text & Dialog</color><br>Text and dialog regarding the object you want the player to defend. Text displays in either the navigation bar or in the chat window. The dialog is spoken by either the enemy group attacking the object or the object itself."




// Name :
"P3357527778" "Defend Object Description"

// ToolTip :
"P2162501430" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Defend Object Description</color><br>The information regarding the defendable object. The description is given when a player right-clicks on the object and selects info.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br><i>This computer contains the secrets of the universe. Defend it with your life. </i></color>"









// ToolTip :
"P3896048281" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Navigation Text (Plural)</color><br>The short description displayed in the navigation bar that pertains specifically to this object. This is the 'plural' description, meaning it's only used if you have more than one of this specific object in the mission (if you set your quantity to something greater than 1). A number is automatically placed in front of this description, so format your text appropriately.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>3 Crates to Defend<br>6 Bombs to Guard<br>2 Computers to Protect</color>"









// ToolTip :
"P2716395303" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Navigation Text (Singular)</color><br>The short description displayed in the navigation bar that pertains specially to this object. This is the 'singular' description, meaning it's used only if you have <b>one</b> object of this type (if you kept the quantity of this object set at one or if there is only one left in the mission).<br><br>Unlike the plural version of this description, the singular does not place a number in front of the text. So, you'll have to add it in if that's what you want.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>1 Computer to Defend<br>Defend Last Crate<br>Only 1 Safe Left...</color>"








// Name :
"P3388985018" "Object Defended Text"

// ToolTip :
"P524848421" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Object Defended Text</color><br>This text displays in the chat window once an object has been successfully defended, meaning the player has defended all of the objects of this type.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>You have defended all the computers. Return to your contact for further instruction.</color>"






// Name :
"P1263072358" "Attacker 1 Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P364678517" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Attacker 1 Dialog</color><br>Dialog spoken by one of the attackers as they approach the object they seek to destroy.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown><i>We have to destroy that object.</i></color>"







// Name :
"P3318215557" "Attacker 2 Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P2728153576" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Attacker 2 Dialog</color><br>Dialog spoken by one of the attackers as the approach the object they seek to destroy.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown><i>Not to worry. This thing is going to be in pieces when we're done with it.</i></color>"







// Name :
"P1900163366" "Attacker Alerted Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P2073022257" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Attacker Alerted Dialog</color><br>Dialog spoken by one of the attackers when they become aware of the player's presence around the object.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown><i>There it is! That's what we're meant to destroy.</i></color>"








// Name :
"P3722780432" "Object Unaware Dialog"


// ToolTip :
"P1191177531" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Object Unaware Dialog</color><br>Dialog spoken by the enemies attacking the object before they are aware of the player character.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown><i>Let's blow this thing.</i></color>"






// Name :
"P1970989979" "Object Alerted Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P228107203" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Enemy Group Attack Dialog</color><br>Dialog spoken by the enemies attacking the object once they are aware of the player character.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown><i>Someone's here!</i></color>"







// Name :
"P1534676185" "Object At 3/4 Health Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P3719152485" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Object At 3/4 Health</color><br>Dialog spoken by the object when it's 3/4 destroyed. <br><br>Note, this dialog will appear above the object as if it is actually talking to the player. For most cases, an inanimate object talking will seem odd to the player, but there are some instances where this might be useful. Use it accordingly."







// Name :
"P1245141589" "Object 1/2 Destroyed"

// ToolTip :
"P3804196014" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Object 1/2 Destroyed</color><br>Dialog spoken by the object when it's half destroyed. <br><br>Note, this dialog will appear above the object as if it is actually talking to the player. For most cases, an inanimate object talking will seem odd to the player, but there are some instances where this might be useful. Use it accordingly."







// Name :
"P2726465558" "Object 1/4 Destroyed"

// ToolTip :
"P1405975212" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Object 1/4 Destroyed</color><br>Dialog spoken by the object when it's 1/4 destroyed. <br><br>Note, this dialog will appear above the object as if it is actually talking to the player. For most cases, an inanimate object talking will seem odd to the player, but there are some instances where this might be useful. Use it accordingly."







// Name :
"P179292786" "Object Destroyed"

// ToolTip :
"P1620590377" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Object Destroyed</color><br>Dialog spoken by the object as it's destroyed. <br><br>Note, this dialog will appear above the objects head as if it is actually talking to the player. For most cases, an inanimate object talking will seem odd to the player, but there are some instances where this might be useful. Use it accordingly."












// DisplayName :
"P4062270863" "A Destructible Object"

// Tooltip :
"P3474537270" "<color DeepSkyBlue>A Destructible Object</color><br>This is an object the players must destroy. They must also defeat any enemies guarding the object as well. <br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br>Somewhere in this warehouse is a cursed relic that if not destroyed will doom the world.</color>"








// Name :
"P2534562428" "Destructible Object Name"

// ToolTip :
"P36719835" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Destroy Object Name</color><br>The name of the object. Players will see this name when they click on the object. It will also be the name you will use when sending the players into the mission to destroy said object.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>Ancient Lockbox<br>Medical Equipment<br>All Your Worldly Possessions.</color>"







// Name :
"P2381962338" "Destructible Object List"

// ToolTip :
"P651539223" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Destroy Object List</color><br>The list of possible objects that can be destroyed.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>Ancient Lockbox<br>Clockwork Parts<br>Ancient Tablet</color>"











// ToolTip :
"P4257011817" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Destructible Settings</color><br>These settings are not required for this goal to be playable."





// ToolTip :
"P1746528821" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Required for Mission Complete</color><br>If this option is turned on, the mission goal must be completed for the mission to complete. If it's turned off, the player does not need to destroy this object in order for the mission to complete."
























// ToolTip :
"P2372214506" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Quantity</color><br>The number of this type of destructible objects you want to in your mission. This will make multiple copies of this object in the mission.<br><br>Note that if you use this option, the object, description, placement, all of it will be exactly the same. Traditionally, this is only useful for the more generic objects you want to have in a map to fill out the space."




















// Name :
"P4054000551" "Guarding Enemy Group"

// ToolTip :
"P1557718942" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Guarding Enemy Group</color><br>The enemy group guarding the object you want the player character to destroy."




































// ToolTip :
"P627712263" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Enemy Group Difficulty</color><br>The difficulty of the enemies in guarding the object. Increasing the difficulty adds enemies of higher ranks into the group, more lieutenants as opposed to minions or more bosses as opposed to lieutenants, etc."









// ToolTip :
"P1863391442" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Starting Animation</color><br>The animation of the enemy group guarding the object when first encountered.<br><br>Note: Regretfully, not all animations work for all entities."











// ToolTip :
"P341362421" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Destructible Text & Dialog</color><br>Text and dialog regarding the object you want the player to destroy. Text displays in either the navigation bar or in the chat window. The dialog is spoken by either the enemy group guarding the object or the object itself."




// Name :
"P784709849" "Destructible Object Description"

// ToolTip :
"P1516636976" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Destructible Object Description</color><br>The information regarding the destructible object. The description is given when a player right-clicks on the object and selects info.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br><i>This lock box is without a key. Smashing it open is the only way to get what you need out of it. </i></color>"









// ToolTip :
"P812214487" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Navigation Text (Plural)</color><br>The short description displayed in the navigation bar that pertains specifically to this object. This is the 'plural' description, meaning it's only used if you have more than one of this specific object in the mission (if you set your quantity to something greater than 1). A number is automatically placed in front of this description, so format your text appropriately.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>3 Crates to Destroy<br>6 Bombs to Blow<br>2 Computers to Smash</color>"









// ToolTip :
"P1535091320" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Navigation Text (Singular)</color><br>The short description displayed in the navigation bar that pertains specially to this object. This is the 'singular' description, meaning it's used only if you have <b>one</b> object of this type (if you kept the quantity of this object set at one or if there is only one left in the mission).<br><br>Unlike the plural version of this description, the singular does not place a number in front of the text. So, you'll have to add it in if that's what you want.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>1 Computer Remains<br>Destroy Last Display Case<br>Only 1 Safe Left...</color>"







// Name :
"P255279334" "Object Destroyed Text"

// ToolTip :
"P2065230842" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Object Destroyed Text</color><br>This text displays in the chat window once the object is destroyed, meaning the player has destroyed all of the objects of this type.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>You have destroyed all the computers. Return to your contact for further instruction.</color>"






// Name :
"P1099190974" "Guards Unaware Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P2981886686" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Enemy Unaware Dialog</color><br>Dialog spoken by the enemy before they are aware of the player character.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown><i>No one can get past us.</i></color>"






// Name :
"P3190967070" "Enemy Attack Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P515844796" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Enemy Group Attack Dialog</color><br>Dialog spoken by the enemy when they are aware of the player character.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown><i>We have to defend this object at all cost.</i></color>"








// ToolTip :
"P797839537" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Object Unaware Dialog</color><br>Dialog spoken by the object before it's aware of the player character.<br><br>Note, this dialog will appear above the object as if it is actually talking to the player. For most cases, an inanimate object talking will seem odd to the player, but there are some instances where this might be useful. Use it accordingly."







// Name :
"P532235243" "Object Aware Dialog"








// Name :
"P1581015378" "Object 3/4 Destroyed Dialog"

































// Name :
"P305548016" "Object Destroyed Clue"


// ToolTip :
"P2849650178" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Object Destroyed Clue</color><br>The clue granted on destruction of the object. Clues are helpful to progress the story, giving more information directly related to the object."




// ToolTip :
"P86100923" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Clue Name</color><br>The name of the clue that appears in the clue window for the player. <br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>Lockbox Contents<br>Data Chip<br>The plot thickens</color>"







// ToolTip :
"P3233794288" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Clue Description</color><br>The actual text of the clue. The player will get this description from their clue window.<br><br>Example: <color SandyBrown>Upon destroying the lockbox you find a data chip that somehow survived. You're not sure what it contains just yet but you bet it has something to do with the missing girl.</color>"













// DisplayName :
"P207038023" "Patrol"

// Tooltip :
"P2281623209" "<color DeepSkyBlue>A Patrol</color><br>A group of enemies that will wander around an area of the map. These are good for making your map feel more alive as well as fleshing out the story of your mission.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br>As the player enters the map, they notice two guards walking around. One guard says, 'So, you think the boss is actually going through with it?' The other guard says, 'Between you and me, I hope not.'</color>"








// Name :
"P1920652735" "Patrol Name"

// ToolTip :
"P2869546690" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Patrol Name</color><br>The name of the patrol. This name is for your use only. The players will never see it.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>Front Outcast Patrol</color>"




















// Name :
"P3583939748" "Patrol Enemy Group"

// ToolTip :
"P816959773" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Patrol Enemy Group</color><br>The enemy group you want for the patrol."





























// ToolTip :
"P154605639" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Settings</color><br>These settings are not required for the mission to be playable."














// ToolTip :
"P605387905" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Quantity</color><br>The amount of this specific type of patrol you want to in your mission. This will make multiple copies of the patrol in the mission.<br><br>Note that if you use this option, the enemy group, dialog and placement will be exactly the same. Traditionally, this is only useful for the more generic patrols you want to have in a map to fill out the space."







// Name :
"P4046427308" "Patrol Alignment"

// ToolTip :
"P1947227315" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Patrol Alignment</color><br>Sets the alignment of your patrol. Alignment determines what 'team' the patrol is on during the mission.<br><br>Ally: <color SandyBrown>The patrol will actually be your friend and the the enemy of all other spawns on the map.</color><br>Enemy: <color SandyBrown>The patrol is the enemy of the player, but not the of the rest of the spawns on the map. Default.</color><br>Rogue: <color SandyBrown>The patrol is no one's friend. Not yours or the other enemies on the map. They'll fight everything they come across"







// Name :
"P2503671806" "Patrol Placement"

// ToolTip :
"P2319846846" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Patrol Placement</color><br>The location on the map that the patrol will spawn.<br><br>Any: <color SandyBrown>The game will pick a random location from Front, Middle or Back to appear.</color><br>Back: <color SandyBrown>The patrol will spawn in the back of the mission map.</color><br>Front: <color SandyBrown>The patrol will spawn in the front of the map.</color><br>Middle: <color SandyBrown>The patrol will spawn in the middle of the map.</color>"







// Name :
"P101416057" "Patrol Difficulty"

// ToolTip :
"P1362899309" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Patrol Difficulty</color><br>The difficulty of the enemies in the patrol. Increasing the difficulty adds enemies of higher ranks into the patrol, more lieutenants as opposed to minions or more bosses as opposed to lieutenants, etc."









// Name :
"P828545962" "Patrol Dialog"


// ToolTip :
"P191553162" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Patrol Dialog</color><br>Dialog that you can add to a patrol, but it's not required for this mission goal to be playable."




// Name :
"P3854068188" "Patroller 1 Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P265486315" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Patroller 1 Dialog</color><br>The dialog spoken by one of the members of the patrol.<br><br>Example: <color SandyBrown><i>I've heard we should expect trouble tonight.</i></color>"







// Name :
"P1798794815" "Patroller 2 Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P2531559526" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Patroller 2 Dialog</color><br>The dialog spoken by one of the members of the patrol.<br><br>Example: <color SandyBrown><i>I'm ready for trouble. Bring it.</i></color>"












// DisplayName :
"P382976372" "Release Captive"

// Tooltip :
"P2519781276" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Release Captive</color><br>A captive is someone who you must go into the map and free from surrounding enemies. Once the captive is free, they will flee to the nearest exit. They can't be killed and will not fight with you. For that, use an Escort or Ally mission goal."








// Name :
"P4039449758" "Captive Name"

// ToolTip :
"P1232056126" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Captive Name</color><br>The name of the person you want for this mission goal. This will appear above their head and should also be used in the mission intro and send off dialog to help direct the player to this individual."








// Name :
"P574109105" "Captive Type"

// ToolTip :
"P3110451485" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Captive Type</color><br>There are two types of captive goals.<br><br>Standard: <color SandyBrown>People that already exist in the game for you to pull from.</color><br>Custom Captive: <color SandyBrown>Captives that you've created yourself to add into the mission.</color>"











// Name :
"P2478488017" "Captive Group"

// ToolTip :
"P4111316909" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Captive Group</color><br>Like enemies, Captives are also associated with a group. Here you select the group of which your captive is a part."
















// Name :
"P3215171730" "Custom Captive Group"

// ToolTip :
"P1706038391" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Custom Captive Group</color><br>This is the group of which your custom captive is a part. Similar to enemy groups, custom captives are also associated with a group as well."














// ToolTip :
"P785404164" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Release Captive Settings</color><br>These settings are not required for this mission goal to be playable."





// ToolTip :
"P2363255207" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Required for Mission Complete</color><br>If this option is turned on, the mission goal must be completed for the mission to complete. If it's turned off, the player does not need to rescue this person in order for the mission to complete."























// ToolTip :
"P3879072661" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Quantity</color><br>The amount of this specific type of captive you want to in your mission. This will make multiple copies of the captive in the mission.<br><br>Note that if you use this option, the name, enemy groups, model of the person, description, placement, all of it will be exactly the same. Traditionally, this is only useful for the more generic people you want to have in a map to fill out the space."




















// ToolTip :
"P383915492" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Enemy Group</color><br>The enemy group surrounding the person. In most cases this is the enemy group holding the captive hostage in the case of a hero mission or trying to protect the person in the case of a villain kidnap mission."



























// Name :
"P2775128866" "Captive Placement"

// ToolTip :
"P4134032034" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Captive Placement</color><br>The location on the map that the captive will spawn.<br><br>Any: <color SandyBrown>The game will pick a random location from Front, Middle or Back to appear.</color><br>Back: <color SandyBrown>The captive will spawn in the back of the mission map.</color><br>Front: <color SandyBrown>The captive will spawn in the front of the map.</color><br>Middle: <color SandyBrown>The captive will spawn in the middle of the map.</color>"








// ToolTip :
"P2574465046" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Enemy Group Difficulty</color><br>The difficulty of the enemies in guarding the captive. Increasing the difficulty adds enemies of higher ranks into the group, more lieutenants as opposed to minions or more bosses as opposed to lieutenants, etc."








// Name :
"P4260606834" "Surrounding Group Alignment"

// ToolTip :
"P1000966340" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Surrounding Group Alignment</color><br>Set the alignment of the enemy group surrounding the captive. If this enemy group is set to Ally, the player will NOT be able to rescue the captive. The group won't be attackable. If the enemy group is set to Rogue, other enemies on the map could defeat this group before the player actually gets to the person, making the mission much easier to complete than likely intended. So, basically, keep this at enemy unless you have a really good reason to change it."










// Name :
"P30917982" "Release Captive Text & Dialog"


// ToolTip :
"P3872577642" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Release Captive Text & Dialog</color><br>This text and dialog is not required for the mission goal to be playable."





// ToolTip :
"P2465127765" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Captive Group</color><br>The display group of your captive."







// Name :
"P4276062821" "Captive Description"

// ToolTip :
"P1377408476" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Captive Description</color><br>The description or bio of your rescue person. The description is given when a player right-clicks on the person and selects info.<br><br>Example:<color SandyBrown><br><i>This poor girl is the sister of your contact. She wants nothing more than to be home, safe with her family.</i></color>"









// ToolTip :
"P1159788639" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Navigation Text (Plural)</color><br>The short description displayed in the navigation bar that pertains specifically to this captive. This is the 'plural' description, meaning it's only used if you have more than one of this specific person in the mission (if you set your quantity to something greater than 1). A number is automatically placed in front of this description, so format your text appropriately.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>3 Hostages to Rescue<br>6 Victims to Kidnap<br>2 Allies to Find</color>"









// ToolTip :
"P2284117722" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Navigation Text (Singular)</color><br>The short description displayed in the navigation bar that pertains specially to this captive. This is the 'singular' description, meaning it's used only if you have <b>one</b> person of this type (if you kept the quantity of this object set at one or if there is only one left in the mission).<br><br>Unlike the plural version of this description, the singular does not place a number in front of the text. So, you'll have to add it in if that's what you want.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>1 Hostage Remains<br>Find Last Journalist<br>Only 1 Victim to kidnap...</color>"







// Name :
"P3818571427" "Release Captive Completed Text"

// ToolTip :
"P3902947723" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Release Captive Completed Text</color><br>This text displays in the chat window once the Release Captive goal is complete.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>You have rescued all the hostages. Return to your contact for further instruction.</color>"







// Name :
"P1904132732" "Enemy Unaware Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P2466518091" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Enemy Unaware Dialog</color><br>Dialog spoken by the enemies surrounding the captive before they are aware of the player character.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown><i>We're going to get a lot of money for you.</i></color>"








// ToolTip :
"P2604369351" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Enemy Group Attack Dialog</color><br>Dialog spoken by the enemies surrounding the captive once they are aware of the player character.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown><i>I guess we're not getting that ransom after all.</i></color>"







// Name :
"P743743554" "Captive Inactive Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P1226029907" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Captive Inactive Dialog</color><br>Dialog spoken by the captive before he/she sees the player."







// Name :
"P1731264722" "Captive Active Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P3219063766" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Captive Active Dialog</color><br>Dialog spoken by the captive upon seeing the player."







// Name :
"P3500593485" "Person Rescued Dialog"

// ToolTip :
"P249607646" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Captive Rescued Dialog</color><br>Dialog spoken by the captive upon being rescued by the player."








