"P807624283" "Rescue Captive Animation"

// ToolTip :
"P2563184568" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Rescue Captive Animation</color><br>The animation played by the captive when rescued.<br><br>Note: Regretfully, not all animations work for all entities."








// Name :
"P3449227369" "Captive Rescued Clue"


// ToolTip :
"P4166044897" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Captive Rescued Clue</color><br>This clue is granted to the player once they've rescued or completed the mission goal involving this captive. Clues are helpful to progress the story, giving more information directly related to this person."




// ToolTip :
"P2993444220" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Clue Name</color><br>The name of the clue that appears in the clue window for the player. <br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown>The Hostage's Account<br>Pleas from your Captives<br>A Tale Told by a Hero</color>"







// ToolTip :
"P3978013300" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Clue Description</color><br>The actual text of the clue. The player will get this description once they've completed this mission goal. <br><br>Example: <color SandyBrown>Once you rescued the little sister she revealed to you that it was in fact your contact who sold her off to a faction of the Outcasts. Apparently, your contact needed the money.</color>"














// DisplayName :
"P2746236723" "Ally"

// Tooltip :
"P2770724933" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Ally</color><br>An Ally is a person the players come across on the map who can aid them in combat.<br><br>Example:<br><color SandyBrown> The players come across Positron being held captive by a number of Crey guards. Once you free him he stands up and says, 'Come on. Let's shut this place down.'</color>"








// Name :
"P3591105958" "Ally Name"

// ToolTip :
"P2579678727" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Ally Name</color><br>The name of the person you want for this mission goal. This will appear above their head and should also be used in the mission intro and send off dialog to help direct the player to this individual."








// Name :
"P83281033" "Ally Type"

// ToolTip :
"P77474347" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Ally Type</color><br>There are two types of ally types.<br><br>Standard: <color SandyBrown>People that already exist in the game for you to pull from.</color><br>Custom Ally: <color SandyBrown>People that you've created yourself to add into the mission.</color>"











// Name :
"P3147747262" "Ally Group"

// ToolTip :
"P43300680" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Ally Group</color><br>Like enemies, allies are also associated with a group. Here you select the group of which your person is a part."














// Name :
"P3340265435" "Custom Ally Group"

// ToolTip :
"P3817235673" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Custom Ally Group</color><br>This is the group of which your custom ally is a part. Similar to enemy groups, custom people are also associated with a group as well."















// ToolTip :
"P264076992" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Ally Settings</color><br>These settings are not required for this mission goal to be playable."





// ToolTip :
"P1757490703" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Required for Mission Complete</color><br>If this option is turned on, the mission goal must be completed for the mission to complete. If it's turned off, the player does not need to find this ally in order for the mission to complete."























// ToolTip :
"P3570059240" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Quantity</color><br>The amount of this specific type of ally you want to in your mission. This will make multiple copies of the ally in the mission.<br><br>Note that if you use this option, the name, enemy groups, model of the person, description, placement, all of it will be exactly the same. Traditionally, this is only useful for the more generic people you want to have in a map to fill out the space."





















// ToolTip :
"P3281611941" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Enemy Group</color><br>The enemy group surrounding the ally. In most cases this is the enemy group holding the person hostage in the case of a hero mission or trying to protect the person in the case of a villain kidnap mission."



























// Name :
"P1376625097" "Ally Placement"

// ToolTip :
"P3334939594" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Ally Placement</color><br>The location on the map that the ally will spawn.<br><br>Any: <color SandyBrown>The game will pick a random location from Front, Middle or Back to appear.</color><br>Back: <color SandyBrown>The ally will spawn in the back of the mission map.</color><br>Front: <color SandyBrown>The ally will spawn in the front of the map.</color><br>Middle: <color SandyBrown>The ally will spawn in the middle of the map.</color>"








// ToolTip :
"P3969796441" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Enemy Group Difficulty</color><br>The difficulty of the enemies in guarding the ally. Increasing the difficulty adds enemies of higher ranks into the group, more lieutenants as opposed to minions or more bosses as opposed to lieutenants, etc."








// Name :
"P933960356" "Ally Behavior"

// ToolTip :
"P111178453" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Ally Behavior</color><br>What the ally does when they are rescued.<br><br>Do Nothing: <color SandyBrown>The ally will simply stand there and do nothing.</color><br>Follow: <color SandyBrown>Once the ally will follow the player.</color><br>Run Away: <color SandyBrown>The ally will run away in fear when rescued.</color><br>Run To Nearest Door: <color SandyBrown>The ally will run away and find the nearest door from which to exit.<br></color>Wander: <color SandyBrown>Upon rescue, the ally will begin to wander around the area."








// Name :
"P3332507179" "Combat Abilities"

// ToolTip :
"P3533371193" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Combat Abilities</color><br>How the ally chooses to fight once rescued. Options include:<br><br>Fight Aggressive: <color SandyBrown>The ally will attack other enemies on the map, often time running away from the player to engage.</color><br>Fight Defensive: <color SandyBrown>The ally will fight other enemies but will remain as close to the player as possible.</color><br>NonCombat: <color SandyBrown> The ally will not fight enemies and enemies will not attempt to fight the person.</color><br>Pacifist: <color SandyBrown>The ally will be attacked by enemies, but will not attack back.</color><br><br> For the cases of Fight Aggressive, Fight Defensive and Pacifist, there is a chance the ally can be defeated."








// Name :
"P3377338064" "Betrays When..."

// ToolTip :
"P4177155291" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Betrays When</color><br>The point at which the ally will turn against the rescuer."




