// Name :
"P1807333049" "Enemy Group Alignment"

// ToolTip :
"P515236448" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Enemy Group Alignment</color><br>Set the alignment of the group which includes the escort being held as well as the group holding the person. This has the following options:<br><br>Default: <color SandyBrown>The person being held is your ally and the surrounding group are your enemies.</color><br>Rogue: <color SandyBrown>The person being held is your enemy as is the surrounding group. This option is possible as a required element for the mission, but if you kill the person the mission will fail.</color>"









// DisplayName :
"P3317451042" "Rogue"











// ToolTip :
"P1908945877" "<color DeepSkyBlue>Combat Abilities</color><br>What the escort does once rescued. Options include:<br><br>Fight Aggressive: <color SandyBrown>The person will attack other enemies on the map, often time running away from the player to engage.</color><br>Fight Defensive: <color SandyBrown>The person will fight other enemies but will remain as close to the player as possible.</color><br>NonCombat: <color SandyBrown> The person will not fight enemies and enemies will not attempt to fight the person.</color><br>Pacifist: <color SandyBrown>The person will be attacked by enemies, but will not attack back.</color><br><br> For the cases of Fight Aggressive, Fight Defensive and Pacifist, there is a chance the person can be defeated. If you set Success On to be Delivery there is a chance the person can be defeated before they reach their destination. In these cases, the player can fail this mission. So, make sure you write any Mission Fail Dialog or Mission Fail Text to account for this."








